1
00:00:01,709 --> 00:00:04,253
Three bounces into this cup.

2
00:00:05,129 --> 00:00:06,172
Three bounces.

3
00:00:06,464 --> 00:00:08,216
- He can do it.
- Won't happen.

4
00:00:11,010 --> 00:00:12,929
You... kiss good-bye to your cash.

5
00:00:19,769 --> 00:00:20,937
- "Nice."
- Never any doubt.

6
00:00:21,395 --> 00:00:24,815
It's a little skill I picked up working
the night shift at San Diego. Thank you.

7
00:00:25,274 --> 00:00:27,109
- You wanna go again?
- Nope.

8
00:00:28,027 --> 00:00:29,070
Do I hear chicken?

9
00:00:30,905 --> 00:00:33,741
- Van Pelt. Line two... O'Laughlin.
- Thanks.

10
00:00:36,410 --> 00:00:37,620
- Go ahead.
- What?

11
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:39,789
You always say something
when O'Loughlin calls.

12
00:00:40,706 --> 00:00:42,250
There's nothing to say.
I'm over it.

13
00:00:43,376 --> 00:00:45,086
Who are you and what have
you done with Wayne Rigsby?

14
00:00:45,378 --> 00:00:46,921
Hey. Anybody see Jane?

15
00:00:48,881 --> 00:00:51,342
{\an8}- "Where are you?"
- I'm boosting team morale.

16
00:00:51,592 --> 00:00:53,427
People are bored.
That needs to be addressed.

17
00:00:53,636 --> 00:00:56,847
People are bored because nobody's
been killed that needs our help.

18
00:00:57,014 --> 00:00:59,225
It's a good thing when homicide
detectives are bored.

19
00:00:59,767 --> 00:01:01,852
So why are you calling me
to find out where I am?

20
00:01:02,103 --> 00:01:04,438
"Because I get nervous
when I don't know where you are."

21
00:01:04,605 --> 00:01:06,274
What do you mean,
"Boosting morale"?

22
00:01:06,857 --> 00:01:08,192
I'm buying fresh fruit...

23
00:01:08,401 --> 00:01:11,320
Clears away the cobwebs,
chases away the blues.

24
00:01:13,489 --> 00:01:16,242
- Good. Get me a red delicious.
- Okay.

25
00:01:19,287 --> 00:01:23,040
"Norberto, where are
the red delicious apples?"

26
00:01:26,752 --> 00:01:29,589
- Let's go. We're going. Come on!
- Okay. Okay.

27
00:02:07,335 --> 00:02:09,503
Golden delicious is fine
if they don't have...

28
00:02:11,130 --> 00:02:12,173
Lisbon!

29
00:02:13,633 --> 00:02:14,717
I'm in trouble here.

30
00:02:17,178 --> 00:02:18,220
Lisbon.

31
00:02:36,153 --> 00:02:37,488
How long ago did you get the call?

32
00:02:37,655 --> 00:02:39,573
- 35 minutes.
- Witnesses?

33
00:02:39,740 --> 00:02:42,576
9-1-1 had some callers.
C.H.P.'s rounding 'em up for us now.

34
00:02:43,035 --> 00:02:45,454
- Jane?
- No sign.

35
00:02:46,121 --> 00:02:48,666
Half a dozen 9-millimeter casings...
3 went into the victim.

36
00:02:48,999 --> 00:02:51,377
{\an8}Got 2 380 casings here.
Looks like one hit.

37
00:02:51,543 --> 00:02:54,129
{\an8}The guy runs a fruit stand.
What's he doing with a 380?

38
00:02:54,338 --> 00:02:55,631
{\an8}He's probably been held up
more than once.

39
00:02:55,798 --> 00:02:57,466
{\an8}Not this time.
Cash register's full.

40
00:02:57,633 --> 00:03:00,177
{\an8}There's a blood trail starting here
heading out into that direction.

41
00:03:00,386 --> 00:03:02,513
{\an8}Looks like whoever the grocer
shot went over to the barn

42
00:03:02,638 --> 00:03:04,264
{\an8}after he took the bullet,
kicked in the door.

43
00:03:04,973 --> 00:03:06,600
{\an8}Jane was there.
So they were after him.

44
00:03:06,975 --> 00:03:09,603
{\an8}Boss, C.H.P. rounded up
the 9-1-1 callers.

45
00:03:09,728 --> 00:03:11,355
This is Harold Keel.
He made the first call.

46
00:03:11,605 --> 00:03:12,940
Did you see the shooting, Mr. Keel?

47
00:03:13,107 --> 00:03:15,984
{\an8}No, just saw two guys in a lot.
One of 'em had a gun.

48
00:03:16,276 --> 00:03:19,071
He was trying to shove the other guy
into the trunk of his car.

49
00:03:19,238 --> 00:03:20,280
{\an8}Can you describe him?

50
00:03:20,406 --> 00:03:23,242
{\an8}The guy with the gun had a sweatshirt
with the hood up.

51
00:03:24,284 --> 00:03:26,495
{\an8}And the other guy was smaller,
in a suit...

52
00:03:26,745 --> 00:03:29,331
No not really a suit,
but like a vest.

53
00:03:32,126 --> 00:03:34,503
- Your name?
- I'm Sherry Winger. I heard the shots.

54
00:03:34,628 --> 00:03:36,797
{\an8}- But you didn't see anything?
- I just heard them while driving by

55
00:03:36,922 --> 00:03:38,215
{\an8}but about a minute later

56
00:03:38,340 --> 00:03:40,092
{\an8}a car booked past me
going about 100.

57
00:03:40,467 --> 00:03:42,261
{\an8}Took the exit ramp on
the highway going north.

58
00:03:42,469 --> 00:03:45,764
- What did the car look like?
- Sedan, brownish-yellow.

59
00:03:45,889 --> 00:03:49,143
{\an8}- You get a look at the license plates?
- I think it was blue and purple.

60
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:52,312
{\an8}- That's an Arizona plate. I'm on it.
- Sergeant?

61
00:03:52,479 --> 00:03:53,522
Yeah?

62
00:03:53,647 --> 00:03:56,275
{\an8}We need a roadblock set up 100 miles north
looking for that car

63
00:03:56,567 --> 00:03:58,152
also an aircraft checking out
the side roads.

64
00:03:58,277 --> 00:04:00,237
{\an8}Have one of your men
stay with both the witnesses

65
00:04:00,446 --> 00:04:01,989
{\an8}and run their licenses.
Make sure they're clean.

66
00:04:02,156 --> 00:04:03,198
You got it.

67
00:04:05,868 --> 00:04:07,786
{\an8}- We need the FBI on this.
- I'll make the call.

68
00:04:08,871 --> 00:04:11,498
If Jane were here, he...
he'd make some snarky remark

69
00:04:11,665 --> 00:04:13,667
{\an8}about something we missed
at the crime scene.

70
00:04:16,336 --> 00:04:17,379
So?

71
00:04:17,963 --> 00:04:19,006
{\an8}What is it?

72
00:04:32,686 --> 00:04:33,729
Hands out.

73
00:04:41,069 --> 00:04:42,362
Looks pretty painful.

74
00:04:43,447 --> 00:04:45,783
- Shut up.
- I could help make that hurt less.

75
00:04:48,494 --> 00:04:49,536
Right.

76
00:04:50,162 --> 00:04:51,955
Hey, what is this about?
Why... Why am I here?

77
00:04:53,415 --> 00:04:54,458
{\an8}Hey...

78
00:04:57,503 --> 00:04:58,545
Hey...

79
00:05:11,975 --> 00:05:13,644
C.H.P.'s got nothing
on the roadblocks yet.

80
00:05:13,769 --> 00:05:15,646
Keep checking. Don't wait
for them to report in.

81
00:05:15,813 --> 00:05:17,356
The phone company's sending
over Jane's records.

82
00:05:17,481 --> 00:05:19,483
Run his calls. We need to know
who he was talking to...

83
00:05:19,608 --> 00:05:20,734
and what he was talking about.

84
00:05:21,109 --> 00:05:23,111
It feels weird to go through Jane's phone.
He'd hate it.

85
00:05:23,237 --> 00:05:24,696
He'll hate it a lot more
if we don't find him.

86
00:05:24,947 --> 00:05:25,989
Teresa.

87
00:05:26,114 --> 00:05:27,407
- I can't talk press right now, Brenda.
- It's about Jane.

88
00:05:27,699 --> 00:05:29,535
- What?
- I'm hearing from reporters.

89
00:05:29,910 --> 00:05:31,286
The highway shutdown's
getting attention.

90
00:05:31,453 --> 00:05:32,663
There are rumors that a CBI

91
00:05:32,788 --> 00:05:34,456
- employee has been killed.
- For God sakes.

92
00:05:34,581 --> 00:05:36,083
Just give me something I can
give 'em to shut 'em up.

93
00:05:36,208 --> 00:05:38,460
We don't know anything yet, Brenda.
Don't say anything.

94
00:05:38,627 --> 00:05:39,670
That just makes it worse.

95
00:05:39,795 --> 00:05:41,755
It's an ongoing investigation.
No comment.

96
00:05:43,674 --> 00:05:45,634
Hey, Lisbon. You remember
agent O'laughlin.

97
00:05:46,009 --> 00:05:47,052
You're the liaison on this?

98
00:05:47,177 --> 00:05:49,596
Any assistance the FBI can offer,
you let me know.

99
00:05:50,055 --> 00:05:52,057
- You think this was Red John?
- I don't see any signs of it.

100
00:05:52,182 --> 00:05:54,351
Red John is clean and efficient.
This was sloppy.

101
00:05:54,518 --> 00:05:56,478
All right, it could be deliberate
keep you off his trail.

102
00:05:56,728 --> 00:05:58,856
Red John already took Jane once
and let him go.

103
00:05:58,981 --> 00:06:01,275
- Why would he take him again?
- He's a psycho.

104
00:06:01,400 --> 00:06:02,568
Who knows why he does
what he does?

105
00:06:02,693 --> 00:06:04,319
Yeah, well, he takes him
a second time

106
00:06:04,528 --> 00:06:05,612
I don't think he's coming back

107
00:06:05,737 --> 00:06:09,241
so let's just assume it's not Red John
until we hear something otherwise.

108
00:06:09,575 --> 00:06:11,577
Rigsby, where are we
with the license plate?

109
00:06:11,702 --> 00:06:13,203
Got a list of cars
with Arizona plates

110
00:06:13,328 --> 00:06:14,538
that have been stopped
and ticketed in the state.

111
00:06:14,663 --> 00:06:16,790
- Getting the names now.
- Cho, ballistics?

112
00:06:16,957 --> 00:06:19,293
Dead end. No matches from the shell
casings we found at the scene.

113
00:06:19,459 --> 00:06:21,628
- Help Rigsby run the Arizona names.
- Already am.

114
00:06:22,129 --> 00:06:24,381
Teresa, I need a statement.

115
00:06:24,673 --> 00:06:26,341
You already have my
statement, Brenda.

116
00:06:26,633 --> 00:06:27,676
What's this about?

117
00:06:27,926 --> 00:06:29,303
If we don't say
something about Jane

118
00:06:29,428 --> 00:06:31,597
there's gonna be rumors and lies
out there until we do.

119
00:06:31,763 --> 00:06:32,806
That's fine with me.

120
00:06:32,931 --> 00:06:34,933
- Not with me.
- Does Jane have money?

121
00:06:35,267 --> 00:06:37,436
Just enough to use.
He doesn't really care about money.

122
00:06:37,603 --> 00:06:39,521
Okay, so this probably isn't
a kidnapping for ransom

123
00:06:39,688 --> 00:06:41,356
which means whoever
did this is motivated

124
00:06:41,481 --> 00:06:43,567
by something personal...
anger, revenge.

125
00:06:45,110 --> 00:06:46,862
- Yeah.
- So it would probably be a good idea

126
00:06:46,987 --> 00:06:48,822
to get Jane's name and
picture out in the media.

127
00:06:49,489 --> 00:06:50,782
Right. Humanize him.

128
00:06:51,658 --> 00:06:52,910
Let them know we're
looking for him.

129
00:06:53,118 --> 00:06:55,120
We shouldn't make a statement
until we know something.

130
00:06:55,245 --> 00:06:57,205
I'm sorry, but that
is not your call.

131
00:06:59,124 --> 00:07:00,167
Okay, Brenda.

132
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:02,836
CBI consultant Patrick
Jane has been taken

133
00:07:02,961 --> 00:07:04,338
by person or persons unknown.

134
00:07:04,463 --> 00:07:06,214
We're investigating
and conducting a search...

135
00:07:06,340 --> 00:07:08,842
an extensive search...
in the area. Okay?

136
00:07:09,134 --> 00:07:10,177
That'll work.

137
00:07:12,262 --> 00:07:13,472
Hey. Are you working this?

138
00:07:13,597 --> 00:07:15,140
Yeah. Sorry, I didn't
get a chance to call.

139
00:07:15,349 --> 00:07:16,850
- It's okay. I'll find you later.
- Right.

140
00:07:23,023 --> 00:07:24,608
We didn't need to share this
with the public.

141
00:07:25,108 --> 00:07:26,151
Yes, we did.

142
00:07:27,569 --> 00:07:29,488
And, Teresa, not saying
something doesn't mean

143
00:07:29,613 --> 00:07:30,948
that something isn't happening.

144
00:07:31,823 --> 00:07:32,866
I know.

145
00:07:34,034 --> 00:07:36,453
So, can you get me a
rundown on his enemies?

146
00:07:37,454 --> 00:07:40,916
You mean, the bad guys?
Or the cops, lawyers...

147
00:07:41,041 --> 00:07:42,417
What, he messed with
cops that badly?

148
00:07:42,709 --> 00:07:46,296
Oh, yes but I don't think a cop
would come after a citizen over Jane.

149
00:07:47,089 --> 00:07:48,465
All right. So what about
his personal life...

150
00:07:48,674 --> 00:07:50,842
- Family, friends, lovers?
- He's a loner.

151
00:07:51,051 --> 00:07:52,344
We're his family, pretty much.

152
00:07:53,679 --> 00:07:55,263
I went through Jane's calls
for the past three weeks.

153
00:07:55,389 --> 00:07:56,765
They're all case-related.
Nothing else.

154
00:07:57,099 --> 00:07:59,017
- Look further back.
- Okay.

155
00:07:59,935 --> 00:08:02,270
Didn't one of Jane's old
psychic clients come after him?

156
00:08:02,437 --> 00:08:03,981
Yeah, we're going
through his client list

157
00:08:04,106 --> 00:08:05,524
but why come after him now?

158
00:08:05,649 --> 00:08:08,568
I mean, it's been so long
since he was in that game.

159
00:08:08,694 --> 00:08:11,947
Right. Which leads us
to the inevitable conclusion.

160
00:08:13,115 --> 00:08:15,450
I think someone Jane put away
is getting back at him.

161
00:08:15,659 --> 00:08:16,702
Maybe they've been released.

162
00:08:16,827 --> 00:08:18,120
Maybe they're reaching out
from prison.

163
00:08:18,286 --> 00:08:19,496
Whichever it is,
we need to go through

164
00:08:19,621 --> 00:08:22,124
every case Jane's worked on
since he came to the CBI.

165
00:08:22,541 --> 00:08:23,792
Van Pelt, start digging.

166
00:08:24,251 --> 00:08:26,461
Whoever did this has probably
been unhappy a long time.

167
00:08:43,395 --> 00:08:44,479
Everything okay?

168
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:48,400
You said... you can
make it hurt less.

169
00:08:50,277 --> 00:08:51,403
Sure. I can do that.

170
00:08:52,154 --> 00:08:53,280
What'd you mean by that?

171
00:08:56,700 --> 00:08:59,995
Pain's in the mind
and that's my specialty.

172
00:09:01,288 --> 00:09:02,706
You got some kind of pill on you?

173
00:09:02,914 --> 00:09:04,624
No. No.

174
00:09:05,167 --> 00:09:07,294
Just relax. Look at me.

175
00:09:08,754 --> 00:09:10,881
Let my voice take
the place of the pain.

176
00:09:12,424 --> 00:09:14,092
Feel the pain getting smaller.

177
00:09:15,218 --> 00:09:18,305
Feel the pain going away.
It's folding in on itself.

178
00:09:19,890 --> 00:09:20,932
Folding...

179
00:09:22,434 --> 00:09:24,102
And you're feeling relaxed...

180
00:09:25,270 --> 00:09:26,396
and calm.

181
00:09:36,740 --> 00:09:37,991
Hello, Patrick.

182
00:09:48,041 --> 00:09:49,125
Do you remember me?

183
00:09:50,710 --> 00:09:51,753
Maybe.

184
00:09:53,922 --> 00:09:55,090
That means you don't.

185
00:09:56,633 --> 00:10:00,220
No, it just means that I
have difficulty talking

186
00:10:00,386 --> 00:10:02,055
when someone is
pointing a gun at me.

187
00:10:02,430 --> 00:10:03,473
Why?

188
00:10:04,474 --> 00:10:06,768
- Does it make you scared?
- Yes, it does.

189
00:10:07,727 --> 00:10:10,146
I don't like being bullied.
Please put the gun down.

190
00:10:11,064 --> 00:10:12,982
I like the look on your face
right now too much.

191
00:10:13,108 --> 00:10:16,152
Then just take a photograph.
Please put the gun down. I...

192
00:10:16,611 --> 00:10:18,238
If you are gonna kill me, then you
would've killed me already.

193
00:10:18,363 --> 00:10:19,989
Whatever you want from me,
you're not gonna get it

194
00:10:20,115 --> 00:10:21,366
unless you put the gun down.

195
00:10:27,122 --> 00:10:28,164
Thank you.

196
00:10:30,208 --> 00:10:31,584
You don't remember me, do you?

197
00:10:33,169 --> 00:10:34,212
Is that strange?

198
00:10:36,256 --> 00:10:38,383
Given the way you're carrying
yourself, I'd be surprised

199
00:10:38,508 --> 00:10:40,135
if your own mother recognized you.

200
00:10:41,136 --> 00:10:43,429
Well, my mother died when I was born
so you're probably right.

201
00:10:44,347 --> 00:10:46,099
Sorry. Bad choice.

202
00:10:49,894 --> 00:10:51,604
Little harsh on your
colleague there.

203
00:10:53,439 --> 00:10:54,566
Who cares about him?

204
00:10:56,693 --> 00:10:58,027
I can't believe this.

205
00:10:58,570 --> 00:10:59,612
You're here.

206
00:10:59,988 --> 00:11:01,656
I mean, you're really...
you're really here.

207
00:11:01,781 --> 00:11:03,241
Yeah. I'm... I'm here.

208
00:11:05,743 --> 00:11:07,078
So what's the plan, Rachel?

209
00:11:10,456 --> 00:11:11,749
So you do know who I am.

210
00:11:12,750 --> 00:11:16,713
How many motherless 23-year-olds
with a slight pigeon-toed stance

211
00:11:16,838 --> 00:11:18,464
and a hint of a new
England childhood

212
00:11:18,590 --> 00:11:19,883
in their voice do
you think I've met?

213
00:11:20,258 --> 00:11:23,344
It was a trick then...
the comment about my mother.

214
00:11:23,887 --> 00:11:25,680
You are a sly one, Mr. Jane.

215
00:11:25,805 --> 00:11:28,850
- This is about your father, isn't it?
- We're not going to talk about this.

216
00:11:29,309 --> 00:11:31,102
We can talk about whatever
you wanna talk about.

217
00:11:31,269 --> 00:11:33,146
- No. We're not gonna talk, period.
- Okay.

218
00:11:33,605 --> 00:11:35,190
I know what you do
when you talk to people...

219
00:11:35,315 --> 00:11:38,151
That gentle hand on their
shoulder, the long look in their eyes.

220
00:11:38,276 --> 00:11:39,485
You're not doing that to me.

221
00:11:40,486 --> 00:11:41,529
I don't know what
you're talking about.

222
00:11:41,654 --> 00:11:42,780
- You think I'm stupid.
- No, I don't.

223
00:11:43,531 --> 00:11:45,491
You think everybody's
stupid except for you.

224
00:11:45,617 --> 00:11:47,118
- You're wrong.
- No. No.

225
00:11:47,493 --> 00:11:49,329
You don't even know
what's going on here.

226
00:11:50,580 --> 00:11:52,749
I am going to kill you.

227
00:11:55,376 --> 00:11:57,295
But I am going to hurt you first.

228
00:12:04,844 --> 00:12:06,596
I have to take my medication now.

229
00:12:18,274 --> 00:12:21,110
"And everyone at CBI
is hoping and working"

230
00:12:21,236 --> 00:12:24,030
{\an8}"for the safe return of our friend
and colleague."

231
00:12:24,572 --> 00:12:27,617
{\an8}"We also want to extend our condolences
to the family of Norberto Rivera"

232
00:12:27,825 --> 00:12:29,535
"who died trying to help Mr. Jane."

233
00:12:30,161 --> 00:12:32,580
"The CBI is offering a $10,000
reward for anyone"

234
00:12:32,705 --> 00:12:35,416
"providing information
leading to the return of Mr. Jane."

235
00:12:35,959 --> 00:12:37,502
"We are going to put up
a phone number."

236
00:12:37,627 --> 00:12:39,963
"We encourage anyone
with relevant information to call."

237
00:12:40,672 --> 00:12:41,714
"Thank you."

238
00:12:43,383 --> 00:12:44,592
These are Jane's cases.

239
00:12:45,009 --> 00:12:46,844
We need a disposition on each case.

240
00:12:47,011 --> 00:12:49,138
Is the suspect in jail?
If not, where are they?

241
00:12:49,305 --> 00:12:51,266
- Then look for anything that sticks out.
- Okay.

242
00:12:52,141 --> 00:12:53,518
- More cases?
- Complaints.

243
00:12:53,643 --> 00:12:55,728
I went down to the outreach
officer in Community Relations

244
00:12:55,853 --> 00:12:57,188
and asked if they
had a file on Jane.

245
00:12:57,438 --> 00:13:00,191
- Looks like there's more than one.
- He has his own filing cabinet.

246
00:13:00,650 --> 00:13:03,444
Have Bob in Admin have his juniors
help you do a preliminary search.

247
00:13:03,569 --> 00:13:04,612
I'll clear it with Hightower.

248
00:13:04,737 --> 00:13:05,780
I got something.

249
00:13:05,905 --> 00:13:07,657
C.H.P. got a call from a rancher
outside Wilton.

250
00:13:07,782 --> 00:13:09,742
Says one of his workers
saw a car on a private road

251
00:13:09,867 --> 00:13:11,286
that runs through his land
a few hours ago.

252
00:13:11,786 --> 00:13:13,788
A farmhand approached the car.
Driver waved a gun at him.

253
00:13:14,122 --> 00:13:15,790
Wilton? That's south
of where Jane was taken.

254
00:13:15,915 --> 00:13:17,125
The witness said
he was going north.

255
00:13:17,458 --> 00:13:18,710
I'll get Wilton P.D.
to check it out.

256
00:13:18,835 --> 00:13:21,254
You go. O'Laughlin,
you mind going with him?

257
00:13:22,463 --> 00:13:24,424
We've already had one
person taken today.

258
00:13:24,549 --> 00:13:25,591
Until we know what's going on

259
00:13:25,717 --> 00:13:27,593
I don't want anyone
going anywhere alone.

260
00:13:28,177 --> 00:13:29,887
- Sure.
- Let's go.

261
00:13:36,102 --> 00:13:38,187
- Thanks for coming along.
- No problem.

262
00:13:40,523 --> 00:13:43,776
- Second set of eyes. Always good.
- Yeah.

263
00:13:46,612 --> 00:13:47,655
I'll drive.

264
00:13:52,201 --> 00:13:53,578
Aren't you working
Jane's case files?

265
00:13:54,746 --> 00:13:56,456
Lisbon wants me to go
through his desk first.

266
00:13:57,248 --> 00:13:58,916
Not that any of this
is getting use anywhere.

267
00:13:59,500 --> 00:14:02,003
- You ever seen where he keeps the key?
- No.

268
00:14:03,463 --> 00:14:05,465
I'll get tech services
to have 'em pop the lock.

269
00:14:05,673 --> 00:14:07,383
Nah, that'll take too long. Here.

270
00:14:17,518 --> 00:14:18,561
Thanks.

271
00:14:19,896 --> 00:14:21,022
Don't tell Jane I did that.

272
00:14:24,108 --> 00:14:25,151
Okay.

273
00:14:26,569 --> 00:14:28,071
Cough drops.

274
00:14:28,905 --> 00:14:29,947
Superglue.

275
00:14:31,616 --> 00:14:34,494
Clippings.
Big help.

276
00:14:34,702 --> 00:14:37,038
Well, it figures Jane's not gonna
keep anything important in the office.

277
00:14:39,374 --> 00:14:40,792
Wait. There's something
else in here.

278
00:14:41,501 --> 00:14:42,543
What do you mean?

279
00:14:43,669 --> 00:14:45,254
It's taped to the
top of the drawer.

280
00:14:57,266 --> 00:14:58,309
You think he's dead?

281
00:15:05,817 --> 00:15:06,859
Cho.

282
00:15:08,069 --> 00:15:09,112
Who?

283
00:15:14,992 --> 00:15:17,203
Hey, boss. Call for you.
Linus Wagner from county jail.

284
00:15:17,328 --> 00:15:19,122
- Line two.
- Linus Wagner?

285
00:15:19,288 --> 00:15:20,331
He says it's about Jane.

286
00:15:24,043 --> 00:15:25,169
Who's Linus Wagner?

287
00:15:25,586 --> 00:15:28,423
He's this creepy doctor that Jane put away
a couple years ago.

288
00:15:28,673 --> 00:15:29,715
He... he killed two people

289
00:15:29,841 --> 00:15:31,592
and tried to make it look like
Red John did it.

290
00:15:39,517 --> 00:15:40,560
This is Lisbon.

291
00:15:41,310 --> 00:15:44,021
Agent. Dr. Linus Wagner.
How are you?

292
00:15:44,439 --> 00:15:45,481
What's this about?

293
00:15:45,648 --> 00:15:48,860
"I happened to see on the TV
in our recreation area"

294
00:15:48,985 --> 00:15:50,987
the announcement
about Patrick Jane.

295
00:15:51,863 --> 00:15:53,906
Very sorry to hear it.
I hope he's all right.

296
00:15:54,323 --> 00:15:57,285
Yeah, I'm sure. Do you
have information about him?

297
00:15:57,618 --> 00:15:59,704
"Yes. Yes, I think I may."

298
00:16:00,204 --> 00:16:02,790
Why don't you come out here,
and we can talk about it?

299
00:16:03,249 --> 00:16:04,292
Just tell me.

300
00:16:05,126 --> 00:16:07,587
No. You should come.

301
00:16:09,589 --> 00:16:10,798
It's complicated.

302
00:16:24,187 --> 00:16:26,397
- Mr. Mendoza?
- Yeah?

303
00:16:27,482 --> 00:16:29,025
Wayne Rigsby, CBI.

304
00:16:29,775 --> 00:16:31,027
You called C.H.P. about the car?

305
00:16:31,402 --> 00:16:33,488
- That's right.
- You could've mentioned it was on fire.

306
00:16:34,780 --> 00:16:37,158
Well, it wasn't. Not... not then.

307
00:16:38,326 --> 00:16:41,370
One of my hands saw a car on our road
with a guy holding a gun

308
00:16:41,496 --> 00:16:42,747
so I called the cops.

309
00:16:43,414 --> 00:16:45,625
A little later I saw smoke,
so I called the Fire Department.

310
00:16:45,958 --> 00:16:47,084
You could've given us a heads-up.

311
00:16:47,710 --> 00:16:49,837
Why? You guys put out fires?

312
00:16:50,046 --> 00:16:52,632
Your guy get a look at the driver?
Can he give us a description?

313
00:16:53,174 --> 00:16:55,218
No. Uh, he said he was
wearing a sweatshirt

314
00:16:55,343 --> 00:16:56,552
with, uh, with the hood up.

315
00:16:59,472 --> 00:17:00,515
Thanks.

316
00:17:01,307 --> 00:17:02,350
I have nothing. You?

317
00:17:03,809 --> 00:17:04,852
Nope.

318
00:17:05,853 --> 00:17:06,896
We got California plates.

319
00:17:07,146 --> 00:17:10,024
Second thing the witness
got wrong. Typical.

320
00:17:10,942 --> 00:17:13,945
Look, they must've brought Jane
here and switched to another car.

321
00:17:15,780 --> 00:17:16,822
Yep. It's stolen.

322
00:17:17,406 --> 00:17:20,159
Forensics can sift the ashes.
We should get back to the office.

323
00:17:22,286 --> 00:17:23,329
Rigsby?

324
00:17:23,788 --> 00:17:25,957
What people don't realize
is when they torch a car

325
00:17:26,582 --> 00:17:27,875
the gas tank goes first.

326
00:17:28,501 --> 00:17:30,044
Whole thing burns back to front.

327
00:17:30,920 --> 00:17:33,381
So the trunk gets incinerated,
but sometimes...

328
00:17:33,798 --> 00:17:35,716
Sometimes stuff up front survives.

329
00:17:35,841 --> 00:17:37,426
Well, the car's stolen.
Paperwork's useless.

330
00:17:38,177 --> 00:17:39,971
The guy who took Jane...
he got shot, right?

331
00:17:40,638 --> 00:17:42,431
So he's driving, and he's bleeding.

332
00:17:42,557 --> 00:17:43,975
He's looking for something
to put on the wound.

333
00:17:44,892 --> 00:17:46,185
What do people do when they're driving

334
00:17:46,394 --> 00:17:49,855
and they're looking for something
in the glove compartment?

335
00:17:54,652 --> 00:17:55,695
This...

336
00:17:57,071 --> 00:17:58,114
We take to forensics.

337
00:17:58,614 --> 00:18:01,617
A fingerprint.
No need. Hold it up.

338
00:18:01,909 --> 00:18:02,952
Why?

339
00:18:03,369 --> 00:18:05,830
Bureau techs can scan
the image into A.F.I.S.

340
00:18:06,122 --> 00:18:08,165
If he's in the system,
we'll have an I.D. In ten minutes.

341
00:18:08,958 --> 00:18:10,001
Nice catch.

342
00:18:12,003 --> 00:18:13,045
Yeah.

343
00:18:13,504 --> 00:18:14,547
Thanks.

344
00:18:16,007 --> 00:18:18,467
The print Rigsby found
matches a guy named Fred Kittel

345
00:18:18,634 --> 00:18:19,885
a thug out of Yuba City.

346
00:18:20,219 --> 00:18:23,180
Arrests for assault, armed robbery,
and attempted murder.

347
00:18:23,973 --> 00:18:25,558
- Where's the Jane connection?
- I can't see one.

348
00:18:25,683 --> 00:18:27,101
He wasn't involved
in any of Jane's cases

349
00:18:27,226 --> 00:18:28,894
and he's never been
questioned by the CBI.

350
00:18:29,186 --> 00:18:31,022
So very likely he's a hired hand.

351
00:18:31,647 --> 00:18:32,898
Somebody checking his residence?

352
00:18:33,107 --> 00:18:35,651
Yuba City P.D. went.
Say it's empty, stripped.

353
00:18:35,818 --> 00:18:37,403
- They're circulating his picture.
- Okay.

354
00:18:37,737 --> 00:18:40,656
Check his family, running buddies,
cellmates, employers.

355
00:18:40,865 --> 00:18:41,949
There's gotta be a connection.

356
00:19:00,426 --> 00:19:01,469
Thank you.

357
00:19:04,263 --> 00:19:05,973
Thank you for making
the trip, agent.

358
00:19:06,682 --> 00:19:07,850
Why am I here, Wagner?

359
00:19:09,894 --> 00:19:14,482
- I, I do hope we can be cordial.
- What's the information?

360
00:19:16,525 --> 00:19:20,071
I've been in contact with the person
behind Jane's disappearance.

361
00:19:20,738 --> 00:19:21,781
Who's that?

362
00:19:23,491 --> 00:19:24,700
First things first.

363
00:19:26,118 --> 00:19:27,161
What do you want?

364
00:19:30,247 --> 00:19:32,541
I don't know if you've
kept up with my trial.

365
00:19:32,708 --> 00:19:37,213
It was long
and... tedious.

366
00:19:37,338 --> 00:19:39,423
Unfortunately, it concluded
with my conviction

367
00:19:39,548 --> 00:19:41,050
on two counts of
first-degree murder

368
00:19:41,175 --> 00:19:44,887
so the death penalty is an option.

369
00:19:45,012 --> 00:19:46,055
That sounds about right.

370
00:19:48,057 --> 00:19:49,850
Sentencing is in a few weeks.

371
00:19:50,184 --> 00:19:54,438
The judge might be convinced
to choose something... lesser.

372
00:19:55,523 --> 00:19:56,941
Life in prison, say.

373
00:19:58,693 --> 00:20:00,569
Preferable, from my point of view

374
00:20:00,820 --> 00:20:05,574
but I need people to
testify on my behalf

375
00:20:06,534 --> 00:20:07,868
to ask for clemency

376
00:20:08,828 --> 00:20:11,372
and who better than a CBI agent?

377
00:20:11,789 --> 00:20:15,334
Clemency?
On what possible grounds?

378
00:20:18,754 --> 00:20:21,882
For compassion's sake and... and...

379
00:20:23,175 --> 00:20:24,218
Humanity

380
00:20:26,137 --> 00:20:29,515
more than any particular
personal worth I might have.

381
00:20:31,434 --> 00:20:34,353
Although I did do a great deal
of good in my time, as you know.

382
00:20:34,478 --> 00:20:35,563
There are villages in Africa...

383
00:20:35,688 --> 00:20:37,815
You killed and mutilated
two people.

384
00:20:38,774 --> 00:20:40,025
I'm aware of that.

385
00:20:46,866 --> 00:20:48,117
If you help us with Jane

386
00:20:48,325 --> 00:20:50,411
we can help make your
life easier in here.

387
00:20:51,412 --> 00:20:53,539
Agent, I'm about to
be put on death row.

388
00:20:53,664 --> 00:20:57,793
Do you really think I care about extra
soap and cheeseburgers?

389
00:21:01,672 --> 00:21:04,467
Your friend Jane is very clever

390
00:21:06,135 --> 00:21:07,428
but I don't think he realizes

391
00:21:07,553 --> 00:21:10,514
the rageful feelings his
trickery can provoke.

392
00:21:12,641 --> 00:21:14,101
I've felt that rage.

393
00:21:15,895 --> 00:21:19,690
I've thought of various unpleasant things
I would do to him

394
00:21:21,484 --> 00:21:25,613
and right now someone is acting
on thoughts like those.

395
00:21:27,615 --> 00:21:29,867
Aren't you worried
what's being done to him?

396
00:21:32,369 --> 00:21:35,623
There are things so much
worse than killing a man.

397
00:21:38,751 --> 00:21:39,794
You can go to hell.

398
00:21:40,419 --> 00:21:42,922
And when they kill you,
I'm gonna be there to watch.

399
00:21:47,051 --> 00:21:48,093
Come on.

400
00:22:18,749 --> 00:22:20,668
I will tell them that
you helped on a case

401
00:22:20,835 --> 00:22:22,169
and ask for clemency

402
00:22:22,962 --> 00:22:25,631
but only if your information
brings Jane back alive.

403
00:22:27,216 --> 00:22:29,718
- I don't control that.
- I don't care.

404
00:22:40,020 --> 00:22:42,106
I've done a lot of writing in here.

405
00:22:43,232 --> 00:22:45,025
The bountiful free time.

406
00:22:46,569 --> 00:22:47,987
A while back,
I published an article

407
00:22:48,112 --> 00:22:50,447
in an online journal
about emotional trauma

408
00:22:50,573 --> 00:22:52,324
and its effect on the psyche.

409
00:22:53,075 --> 00:22:55,369
It included some
observations on Jane.

410
00:22:56,745 --> 00:23:00,583
Not long after
I got a letter from a young woman

411
00:23:00,708 --> 00:23:03,711
who claimed to be a graduate
student in psychology.

412
00:23:04,169 --> 00:23:06,338
She said she was researching Jane

413
00:23:07,256 --> 00:23:09,592
but she didn't know a lick
about psychology.

414
00:23:10,050 --> 00:23:13,387
She was, however
obsessed with Jane...

415
00:23:15,764 --> 00:23:17,850
And exceedingly hostile toward him.

416
00:23:18,392 --> 00:23:19,435
What's her name?

417
00:23:25,566 --> 00:23:26,609
You, uh...

418
00:23:29,111 --> 00:23:30,696
You planning on doing
anything about him?

419
00:23:31,989 --> 00:23:33,032
No.

420
00:23:36,827 --> 00:23:38,162
That's not very hygienic.

421
00:23:39,371 --> 00:23:41,206
You know, maybe you can
just shove him in the corner

422
00:23:41,332 --> 00:23:43,834
before he starts to smell.
I mean, I'd do it myself, but...

423
00:23:44,168 --> 00:23:45,210
No.

424
00:23:46,545 --> 00:23:47,588
Fine.

425
00:23:48,464 --> 00:23:50,716
That smell gets in your drapes,
you're never getting it out.

426
00:23:51,508 --> 00:23:54,553
- You think everything's funny.
- Just the funny things.

427
00:23:56,221 --> 00:23:58,098
You never feel guilty, do you?

428
00:23:58,307 --> 00:24:00,601
I feel guilty every
minute of every day.

429
00:24:02,353 --> 00:24:04,146
See? You did it.

430
00:24:05,314 --> 00:24:07,650
You got me talking again,
trying to mess with my mind.

431
00:24:08,651 --> 00:24:10,736
It's abusive, what you do.

432
00:24:11,362 --> 00:24:12,404
You use people...

433
00:24:13,113 --> 00:24:14,156
Like toys.

434
00:24:16,283 --> 00:24:18,452
No thought for the damage you do

435
00:24:19,286 --> 00:24:20,496
the people you hurt.

436
00:24:21,789 --> 00:24:22,831
I'm sorry about your father.

437
00:24:22,998 --> 00:24:24,541
- Maybe you think you are.
- I am.

438
00:24:24,667 --> 00:24:25,918
No, you're not yet.

439
00:24:29,713 --> 00:24:30,756
You will be.

440
00:24:33,217 --> 00:24:35,052
You ever see a rancher
use a cattle prod?

441
00:24:36,345 --> 00:24:37,680
No. No, Rachel.

442
00:24:37,846 --> 00:24:39,056
Cattle can be stubborn.

443
00:24:39,848 --> 00:24:41,392
Takes a real jolt
to get them going.

444
00:24:42,977 --> 00:24:44,019
It must hurt.

445
00:24:45,562 --> 00:24:46,730
You'll have to let me know.

446
00:24:50,693 --> 00:24:51,735
No.

447
00:24:58,281 --> 00:25:00,701
So Wagner says Sherry Winger
was after Jane...

448
00:25:00,826 --> 00:25:04,621
The girl who was the witness?
I thought C.H.P. checked her out.

449
00:25:04,830 --> 00:25:07,541
Now they're saying the license
and registration are fakes...

450
00:25:07,833 --> 00:25:08,875
Top dollar forgeries.

451
00:25:09,001 --> 00:25:10,669
They never would've caught it if
they hadn't taken a second look.

452
00:25:11,128 --> 00:25:13,839
So do we have any idea
who Sherry Winger really is

453
00:25:14,006 --> 00:25:15,298
or where she is?

454
00:25:15,424 --> 00:25:18,510
No. No. The only thing we know
for sure is that she hated Jane.

455
00:25:18,885 --> 00:25:20,929
Linus gave me copies of
the letters she wrote him.

456
00:25:21,179 --> 00:25:23,390
I gave the originals to forensics
so they could run the paper.

457
00:25:23,557 --> 00:25:25,058
Why would she show up at the scene?

458
00:25:25,183 --> 00:25:26,810
It seems like the last place
she'd wanna be.

459
00:25:26,977 --> 00:25:29,104
Misdirection. She gives us
the wrong license plate...

460
00:25:29,229 --> 00:25:31,023
We head north
instead of going south.

461
00:25:31,189 --> 00:25:33,025
Boss, I've read something
else written by this person.

462
00:25:33,150 --> 00:25:34,192
You sure?

463
00:25:34,317 --> 00:25:35,360
Yeah, there are phrases
that I've seen before.

464
00:25:35,485 --> 00:25:37,404
This one calls Jane a
coyote-like trickster

465
00:25:37,946 --> 00:25:39,197
And in one of these...

466
00:25:44,870 --> 00:25:45,996
Where... here.

467
00:25:48,457 --> 00:25:51,293
In this one.
Calls Jane a trickster, a coyote.

468
00:25:51,793 --> 00:25:53,962
- Who wrote that letter?
- It's from the daughter of Don Bowman.

469
00:25:54,379 --> 00:25:56,214
Get a copy of Sherry
Winger's license.

470
00:25:57,716 --> 00:25:58,759
Who's Don Bowman?

471
00:25:59,092 --> 00:26:01,344
Case from three years ago.
Insurance company executive.

472
00:26:01,511 --> 00:26:03,305
He was writing fake policies
and cashing them in.

473
00:26:03,472 --> 00:26:05,557
Company auditor found out,
so Bowman killed him.

474
00:26:06,516 --> 00:26:07,559
That's Bowman.

475
00:26:07,684 --> 00:26:10,812
- And Jane put him away?
- He had a daughter... Rachel, 19.

476
00:26:10,979 --> 00:26:13,732
He was a single father.
She idolized him. He adored her.

477
00:26:14,024 --> 00:26:15,067
Okay.

478
00:26:15,192 --> 00:26:16,777
Jane forges a letter to Bowman
under Rachel's name.

479
00:26:16,902 --> 00:26:19,029
Claiming she's discovered proof
that he committed the murder.

480
00:26:19,654 --> 00:26:22,699
She's devastated, doesn't know
whether to go to the police or kill herself.

481
00:26:22,991 --> 00:26:26,620
- So Bowman races to his daughter.
- He's so sorry. He did it all for her.

482
00:26:26,745 --> 00:26:27,788
She needs to keep the secret.

483
00:26:27,913 --> 00:26:29,206
And you're there?
Jane has you there?

484
00:26:29,331 --> 00:26:30,874
We got the whole
conversation on tape.

485
00:26:31,333 --> 00:26:33,251
Just checked the records.
Don Bowman and Fred Kittel

486
00:26:33,376 --> 00:26:35,295
were both imprisoned at Corcoran
at the same time.

487
00:26:35,796 --> 00:26:36,838
That's the connection.

488
00:26:36,963 --> 00:26:38,548
- But Bowman couldn't be behind this.
- Why not?

489
00:26:38,715 --> 00:26:40,425
He's dead. Died in prison
about a year ago.

490
00:26:42,511 --> 00:26:43,929
Bowman's dead,
but his daughter isn't.

491
00:26:44,096 --> 00:26:45,305
Is that the driver's license picture?

492
00:26:45,764 --> 00:26:46,807
Look at this.

493
00:26:47,808 --> 00:26:50,435
Let me see that.
Rachel Bowman. Sherry Winger.

494
00:26:50,560 --> 00:26:54,022
Oh, Miss Rachel's had some
work done, but that's her.

495
00:26:54,606 --> 00:26:56,024
- Get her address fast.
- Okay.

496
00:26:58,193 --> 00:27:00,946
You didn't know that my father
died in prison, did you?

497
00:27:01,196 --> 00:27:02,239
No.

498
00:27:05,283 --> 00:27:06,493
Of an infection.

499
00:27:07,619 --> 00:27:10,205
Do you know how
incredibly stupid that is?

500
00:27:10,789 --> 00:27:12,874
Simple antibiotics
could've saved him...

501
00:27:12,999 --> 00:27:16,586
But a prison hospital...
It's... it's a nightmare in there.

502
00:27:18,171 --> 00:27:21,716
They just let him die
but you killed him.

503
00:27:44,156 --> 00:27:47,075
- You know, your anger is misplaced.
- Oh, really?

504
00:27:48,827 --> 00:27:52,789
You can't be angry with your father
so... here I am.

505
00:27:52,914 --> 00:27:55,917
Don't you dare say that.
My father loved me.

506
00:27:56,334 --> 00:28:00,255
He took care of me, provided for me.
I'm all he ever cared about.

507
00:28:00,463 --> 00:28:04,050
Yes, you are, and he wouldn't
want you doing this.

508
00:28:04,926 --> 00:28:06,511
Oh, I think he would be very proud.

509
00:28:10,390 --> 00:28:14,144
He loved me so much
and you made me betray him.

510
00:28:15,645 --> 00:28:16,980
When you were talking to me

511
00:28:18,440 --> 00:28:19,691
asking about me and my dad...

512
00:28:19,816 --> 00:28:22,360
I thought that you were
actually concerned.

513
00:28:24,196 --> 00:28:25,739
I mean, I thought
that you liked me.

514
00:28:43,256 --> 00:28:46,259
You want me to be sorry? Okay.
I am sorry.

515
00:28:49,137 --> 00:28:51,890
I'm sorry that the loss of
your father drove you mad.

516
00:28:53,475 --> 00:28:55,352
But I don't regret
what I did to him.

517
00:28:56,853 --> 00:28:58,897
He was a thief and a murderer.

518
00:29:00,315 --> 00:29:02,484
And I did everything I could
to catch him

519
00:29:03,693 --> 00:29:05,403
because that's just who I am.

520
00:29:17,624 --> 00:29:18,667
- You set?
- Yeah.

521
00:29:18,833 --> 00:29:19,876
Go!

522
00:29:25,548 --> 00:29:26,591
- "Clear!"
- "Clear!"

523
00:29:26,716 --> 00:29:27,801
- "Clear!"
- "Kitchen clear!"

524
00:29:29,594 --> 00:29:30,637
"Second story clear!"

525
00:29:33,974 --> 00:29:35,433
House is empty!
There's dust everywhere!

526
00:29:35,558 --> 00:29:37,394
- It looks like she's been gone for weeks!
- Basement?

527
00:29:37,560 --> 00:29:39,771
- Nothin'!
- All right, let's get forensics in here!

528
00:29:39,896 --> 00:29:41,982
Look for anything that'll tell us
where she went!

529
00:29:42,482 --> 00:29:44,776
And get somebody to turn off
that damn alarm!

530
00:29:49,614 --> 00:29:52,242
There's somebody in my house.
I gotta go.

531
00:29:53,618 --> 00:29:54,661
I'll be back.

532
00:29:54,828 --> 00:29:57,289
Rachel, can you please
move that thing?

533
00:29:58,123 --> 00:29:59,165
Please.

534
00:29:59,541 --> 00:30:01,793
Please. Please,
the stench is unbearable.

535
00:30:01,960 --> 00:30:04,796
Over there, anywhere.
Just please, please move him.

536
00:30:08,049 --> 00:30:09,092
Thank you.

537
00:30:16,516 --> 00:30:17,559
Smell that.

538
00:30:30,530 --> 00:30:31,573
Sorry, pal.

539
00:30:56,598 --> 00:30:58,141
So we got a line on
Fred Kittel's dad.

540
00:30:58,266 --> 00:30:59,726
He's got a place just
south of Diamond Springs.

541
00:30:59,851 --> 00:31:01,311
You and O'Laughlin
go and talk to him.

542
00:31:01,561 --> 00:31:02,812
- Sure.
- I'm gonna head back to the office.

543
00:31:02,979 --> 00:31:04,731
I wanna look at something
in Rachel Bowman's file.

544
00:31:04,939 --> 00:31:06,441
All right, I'll hold down
the fort here.

545
00:31:25,668 --> 00:31:26,878
Jane, where are you?

546
00:31:27,587 --> 00:31:28,922
"Not Jane, Agent."

547
00:31:29,130 --> 00:31:30,924
"Just so you know,
I'm looking right at you."

548
00:31:32,133 --> 00:31:35,637
"Everything will be all right
if you do exactly as I say."

549
00:31:35,762 --> 00:31:40,058
"If not, Jane will be dead
in 15 minutes. Clear?"

550
00:31:40,975 --> 00:31:42,018
Clear.

551
00:31:42,268 --> 00:31:44,729
"Drive another 100 yards
and stop at the cafe."

552
00:32:02,497 --> 00:32:05,542
"Take your gun out of its holster.
Place it on the seat."

553
00:32:07,001 --> 00:32:08,670
"Get out of your car
and close the door."

554
00:32:10,046 --> 00:32:11,089
"Walk away."

555
00:32:12,590 --> 00:32:14,259
"15 minutes, Agent."

556
00:32:27,730 --> 00:32:30,692
"Now walk down the street
and come to the gas station."

557
00:33:00,221 --> 00:33:01,848
Let's go see Patrick.

558
00:33:09,061 --> 00:33:10,521
I want two choppers in the air

559
00:33:10,688 --> 00:33:13,524
at a one square mile perimeter
secured around this site.

560
00:33:13,816 --> 00:33:16,694
No car leaves this area
without being searched!

561
00:33:16,819 --> 00:33:19,447
- Not one!
- We have no I.D. on any vehicle.

562
00:33:19,572 --> 00:33:22,742
The suspect is female,
early 20s, blonde, about 5'7".

563
00:33:22,992 --> 00:33:25,036
She has at least one hostage
and possibly two with her.

564
00:33:25,369 --> 00:33:27,872
Give me a second, okay? Hey.

565
00:33:28,331 --> 00:33:29,957
Grace, the office said
something happened to Lisbon.

566
00:33:30,500 --> 00:33:32,877
She's gone. We think Rachel
took her about 20 minutes ago.

567
00:33:33,336 --> 00:33:34,837
- She got Lisbon.
- When?

568
00:33:34,962 --> 00:33:36,756
- Just now.
- Should we come back?

569
00:33:37,298 --> 00:33:39,217
Hey, boss, do you want
Rigsby and O'Laughlin back?

570
00:33:39,342 --> 00:33:40,968
No. Tell them to finish
what they're doing.

571
00:33:41,886 --> 00:33:42,929
Hightower says no.

572
00:33:44,388 --> 00:33:45,431
Wayne...

573
00:33:45,932 --> 00:33:48,851
I know. I know, Grace.
It's... it's gonna be okay.

574
00:33:49,810 --> 00:33:50,978
"All right. Bye."

575
00:34:17,880 --> 00:34:20,216
Mr. Kittel! This is the police!

576
00:34:20,841 --> 00:34:22,093
Come out with your hands up!

577
00:34:23,636 --> 00:34:26,847
Mr. Kittel? CBI!
Hello?!

578
00:34:51,539 --> 00:34:53,082
Mr. Kittel, put the gun down!

579
00:34:53,499 --> 00:34:55,793
- No way I ain't.
- Put it down now.

580
00:34:56,043 --> 00:34:59,297
Hell, no! You got no right
to be here.

581
00:34:59,547 --> 00:35:00,590
We just wanna talk.

582
00:35:01,507 --> 00:35:04,260
Fine! Talk yourselves
on outta here!

583
00:35:06,012 --> 00:35:07,054
Go on!

584
00:35:08,264 --> 00:35:09,307
Get out.

585
00:35:09,515 --> 00:35:10,558
Go on!

586
00:35:11,559 --> 00:35:13,686
All right.
This is how it's gonna go.

587
00:35:14,312 --> 00:35:16,689
On the count of three
I'm gonna shoot you in the head.

588
00:35:17,398 --> 00:35:18,649
- Rigsby...
- No, it's my deal!

589
00:35:18,941 --> 00:35:20,568
Put the gun down, or on three

590
00:35:20,860 --> 00:35:23,029
I shoot you in the head.
You ready? One...

591
00:35:23,154 --> 00:35:25,615
- Just take it easy, okay?
- Two...

592
00:35:27,450 --> 00:35:28,826
- Three!
- Okay!

593
00:35:30,828 --> 00:35:31,912
Okay.

594
00:35:33,581 --> 00:35:35,875
Why you have to be
such a hard-ass for?

595
00:35:36,834 --> 00:35:40,171
Freddy? I ain't seen
Freddy in six months.

596
00:35:40,963 --> 00:35:44,675
I couldn't tell ya
anything about that son of a bitch.

597
00:35:44,884 --> 00:35:46,802
Do you know what he was doing,
who he was in contact with?

598
00:35:47,345 --> 00:35:48,387
What he was doin'?

599
00:35:49,639 --> 00:35:52,767
Well, the last time I saw him
what he was doing was smokin' weed

600
00:35:53,100 --> 00:35:54,852
and lookin' at porn on my laptop.

601
00:35:55,519 --> 00:35:57,730
You have any idea how we can get in touch
with any of his friends?

602
00:35:58,022 --> 00:35:59,607
No, thank God.

603
00:36:01,651 --> 00:36:03,152
Night crawlers... all of 'em.

604
00:36:04,737 --> 00:36:07,657
There is one good thing, though,
that he did for me recently.

605
00:36:08,324 --> 00:36:11,118
He pissed off my ex... his mother.

606
00:36:11,494 --> 00:36:12,536
How'd he do that?

607
00:36:13,412 --> 00:36:14,830
She don't talk
to him for months.

608
00:36:14,997 --> 00:36:19,543
He shows up, sweet-talks her
into giving him the keys

609
00:36:19,669 --> 00:36:22,672
to the family's hunting cabin.

610
00:36:23,297 --> 00:36:25,466
And then he splits
with all the Xanax.

611
00:36:28,552 --> 00:36:29,720
Oh, I'll tell ya.

612
00:36:29,887 --> 00:36:30,971
I had a laugh.

613
00:36:32,473 --> 00:36:34,308
Where is this cabin exactly,
Mr. Kittel?

614
00:36:36,852 --> 00:36:37,895
Go.

615
00:36:38,104 --> 00:36:39,689
I'm going. I'm going.

616
00:36:52,660 --> 00:36:54,954
Visiting hours. Hey, Lisbon.

617
00:36:55,746 --> 00:36:56,789
Hands.

618
00:36:57,707 --> 00:36:58,749
What's the plan, Rachel?

619
00:36:58,916 --> 00:37:01,377
I get to watch Lisbon die
just like you watched your father die?

620
00:37:01,836 --> 00:37:03,087
- That's right.
- What?!

621
00:37:03,462 --> 00:37:05,798
That's what I thought.
I've been smelling gasoline.

622
00:37:05,923 --> 00:37:07,550
- You burning the place down?
- That's right.

623
00:37:07,717 --> 00:37:09,760
- Rachel, think about this for a minute.
- Oh, I have.

624
00:37:09,927 --> 00:37:12,555
- Oh, she certainly has.
- You're never gonna get away with it.

625
00:37:12,888 --> 00:37:14,432
You'll never know if I do or don't.

626
00:37:15,516 --> 00:37:18,519
Lisbon, I'm sorry.
This is my fault.

627
00:37:20,229 --> 00:37:24,316
I will not let you burn alive
as God is my witness.

628
00:37:25,484 --> 00:37:26,527
Good-bye.

629
00:37:26,902 --> 00:37:29,613
Rachel. Rachel, wait! Rachel!

630
00:37:30,281 --> 00:37:32,825
- You're wasting your energy.
- You have a better idea?

631
00:37:32,950 --> 00:37:34,160
Just so happens I do.

632
00:37:35,619 --> 00:37:36,662
Where'd you get that?

633
00:37:37,788 --> 00:37:38,831
Him.

634
00:37:45,921 --> 00:37:48,799
I was hoping to unlock my handcuffs

635
00:37:49,091 --> 00:37:51,635
but, uh, no luck.

636
00:37:51,802 --> 00:37:52,887
Well, what are you gonna do?

637
00:37:54,305 --> 00:37:55,389
You're not gonna like it.

638
00:38:10,654 --> 00:38:11,781
"Help!"

639
00:38:14,784 --> 00:38:19,538
"Help! Help! Help!"

640
00:38:28,714 --> 00:38:29,799
What did you do?

641
00:38:30,257 --> 00:38:31,842
I said I wouldn't let her burn.

642
00:38:32,510 --> 00:38:34,053
This way she won't suffer.

643
00:38:37,223 --> 00:38:38,390
Son of a bitch!

644
00:38:39,725 --> 00:38:41,268
You think I won't hurt you more?

645
00:38:43,354 --> 00:38:46,190
I can do this all night!

646
00:38:50,778 --> 00:38:52,571
Get the gun! Get it!

647
00:38:52,822 --> 00:38:53,989
Get the gun!

648
00:38:57,868 --> 00:38:58,911
To hell with this.

649
00:39:05,251 --> 00:39:06,293
You all right?

650
00:39:09,505 --> 00:39:12,716
Uh... I think I need a shower.

651
00:39:20,099 --> 00:39:21,141
"Rigsby."

652
00:39:22,309 --> 00:39:23,477
- Hi.
- Hey.

653
00:39:24,228 --> 00:39:27,147
I'm heading out, and, uh,
just wanted to say...

654
00:39:28,440 --> 00:39:29,483
It's a good day.

655
00:39:30,067 --> 00:39:31,110
Yeah.

656
00:39:31,861 --> 00:39:34,405
"I'm gonna kill you on the count of three"
was a little out of the box.

657
00:39:35,072 --> 00:39:38,659
- Well, it worked.
- Yeah, it... it did.

658
00:39:39,910 --> 00:39:40,953
Look...

659
00:39:41,078 --> 00:39:43,247
What I really wanted
to say is, uh...

660
00:39:44,623 --> 00:39:45,666
I hope we're cool.

661
00:39:46,250 --> 00:39:48,252
Yeah, 'cause you... you did
some outstanding work.

662
00:39:49,712 --> 00:39:50,754
Yeah.

663
00:39:52,006 --> 00:39:53,048
Yeah, we are.

664
00:39:53,716 --> 00:39:54,758
Appreciate that.

665
00:39:55,843 --> 00:39:56,886
Okay.

666
00:39:57,386 --> 00:39:58,429
See you around.

667
00:40:07,104 --> 00:40:08,689
- O'Laughlin.
- Yeah.

668
00:40:10,482 --> 00:40:11,525
Don't hurt her.

669
00:40:14,945 --> 00:40:15,988
Or what?

670
00:40:16,488 --> 00:40:17,740
Or you'll have to deal with me.

671
00:40:27,458 --> 00:40:29,335
- You okay?
- Good. Thank you.

672
00:40:30,502 --> 00:40:31,712
You're looking a little creaky.

673
00:40:32,504 --> 00:40:33,547
Yeah.

674
00:40:34,340 --> 00:40:36,175
Well, a cattle prod
will do it to you.

675
00:40:36,300 --> 00:40:38,510
Well, the doctor says
there's no lasting effects.

676
00:40:39,386 --> 00:40:41,555
Well, that doctor should
try it himself sometime.

677
00:40:44,141 --> 00:40:45,267
Well, that was a big smile.

678
00:40:48,312 --> 00:40:50,314
Of course I'm glad you're back

679
00:40:50,814 --> 00:40:52,816
but I'm also glad we finally
solved one without you.

680
00:40:54,485 --> 00:40:56,403
You were kidnapped
and delivered to me.

681
00:40:57,488 --> 00:40:58,697
That counts as solving one?

682
00:40:58,864 --> 00:41:00,616
Hightower and the team found us.

683
00:41:00,908 --> 00:41:01,992
But if I hadn't held off Rachel

684
00:41:02,117 --> 00:41:04,161
they would have found us
dead in a burned out house.

685
00:41:04,286 --> 00:41:07,414
Oh, you held off Rachel.
Where's my apple?

686
00:41:08,248 --> 00:41:09,458
- Your what?
- My apple.

687
00:41:09,583 --> 00:41:10,626
I asked you
to get me an apple.

688
00:41:11,126 --> 00:41:13,170
I come through the valley of death
and all you can think about

689
00:41:13,295 --> 00:41:15,798
- is your stomach... a piece of fruit.
- That's right.

690
00:41:16,048 --> 00:41:17,091
- An apple.
- Yes.

691
00:41:17,216 --> 00:41:18,676
- Well, that's just plain selfish.
- Selfish?

692
00:41:18,884 --> 00:41:20,344
- Yes, it is. Now I...
- Me, selfish?

693
00:41:21,011 --> 00:41:22,262
You're on my couch.

694
00:41:22,513 --> 00:41:25,599
I'm trying to have a cup of tea.
Have you finished?

695
00:41:25,766 --> 00:41:28,602
You call me creaky.
I've been cattle-prodded all week.

696
00:41:28,769 --> 00:41:30,437
I just wanna have a
rest and a cup of tea

697
00:41:30,562 --> 00:41:32,982
- and a little sleep.
- Wish I had a cattle prod.

